# T-1000: Map constructor type annotation (type-system-health-s841-followup)
# Verifies that [Map String Int] works as a type annotation on a dict-entry key.
# Map is a Kind::Arrow (arity 2) builtin type constructor registered in kind_env.
# The annotation is accepted by the type checker; at runtime the key resolves to
# the bare name "cache" (Annotated keys strip the annotation).
[
  # Annotate a variable with Map String Int — the annotation is type-checker only.
  # At runtime this is just a dict entry with key "cache".
  cache@[Map String Int]: [name: 1  age: 42  city: 3]

  # get takes (key, collection): get "age" cache
  result: [get "age" cache]
]

---

%.result
=== out
Int(42)
